keep it simple, no flintstones. a torch becomes a burning torch if it is
wielded and comes in contact with fire (magic trap, scroll, wand,
monsters). a burning torch dipped into water (potion, fountain, pool)
would go out. the dipped into (or directionally applied at) item would
disappear as necessary. a burning torch would also, as you suggest, go out
on its own after some time. as mentioned above, merely unwielding the
burning torch would put it out (else i would think it would do fire damage
to your inventory).  a torch can be re-lit, adds utility to scrolls of fire.
